    "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/3185/0/473672/15539/assistant-professor-in-international-development-quantitative-social-science": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in International Development (Quantitative Social Science)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in International Development (Quantitative Social Science) Register Login Back to search results Assistant Professor in International Development (Quantitative Social Science) LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university As an equal opportunities employer strongly committed to diversity and inclusion, we encourage applications from those of Minority Ethnic backgrounds and Women as they are currently under-represented at this level in this area. All appointments will be made on merit or skill and experience relative to the role. Department of International Development Assistant Professor in International Development (Quantitative Social Science) Salary is no less than £68,087 per annum and the salary scale can be found on the LSE website The Department of International Development invites applications for an Assistant Professor in International Development (Quantitative Social Science). We are a vibrant multidisciplinary department seeking candidates with the potential to perform world-class research and teaching on contemporary development problems while working within and advancing social science disciplines. The successful candidate will teach students across all our MScs. The successful candidate will be expected to conduct cutting-edge social science research on development using quantitative methods beyond mainstream economics, such as, for example, a strong disciplinary or multidisciplinary training in economic history, political science, sociology, anthropology, geography, statistics or data science relevant to international development. The role welcomes research addressing themes such as inequality, political stability and instability, governance, and technology and development. Ideally, candidates should have an interest in empirica lly grounded research with fieldwork-based research, and a desire to advance social science theory as evidenced by publications in highly rated social science and development journals or books. Successful applicants will have a PhD or be close to completing a PhD by the start date. They must show a commitment to working in a multidisciplinary environment and contributing to the intellectual life of the School through conducting and publishing outstanding research, engaging in other high-quality teaching as instructed by the Head of Department (including Ph.D. training in time), and participating in the School and wider Departmental activities. The start date is 1 September 2027. Other criteria that will be used when shortlisting for this post can be found on the person specification, which is attached to this va cancy on the LSE’s online recruitment system. In addition to a competitive salary, the benefits that come with this job include an occupational pension scheme, a research grants policy with personal reward options, generous research leave (sabbatical) entitlement, a collegial faculty environment, and excellent support, training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the “contact us” links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Queries about research and teaching in the department may be directed to j.p.faguet@lse.ac.uk. The closing date for receipt of applications is 1 December 2026 (23.59 UK time). W e are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Assistant Professor in International Development (Quantitative Social Science) Job Type: Academic Posted: 01/09/2026 Closing date: 01/12/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
