    "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/1939/0/473549/15539/planning-officer-power-bi-developer": {
      "title": "Planning Officer (Power BI Developer)",
      "description": "Planning Officer (Power BI Developer) Register Login Back to search results Planning Officer (Power BI Developer) LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university Planning Division Planning Officer (Power BI Developer) Salary from £43,277 to £51,714 pa inclusive with potential to progress to £55,497 pa inclusive of London allowance This is fixed term for one year The London School of Economics and Political Science is one of the foremost social science universities in the world. The Planning Division is integral in supporting and monitoring the School’s progress towards achieving its strategic objectives. The Planning Officer (Power BI Developer) supports a range of tasks undertaken across the School, primarily relating to the production of Power BI reports, dashboards and applications to support insight and strategic decision making across the School. Candidates should have: Experience designing and maintaining high‑quality visualisation reports, dashboards and applications. Experience of ETL processes using Alteryx, PowerQuery (M) or Fabric tools (e.g. Dataflows, Lakehouse, pipelines) to create reliable datasets for reporting. Experience developing and managing robust semantic models (dimensional/star schema) to underpin scalable and reusable reporting solutions including DAX optimisation and model design best practice. Experience working with end-users and stakeholders to translate business requirements into data models, measures and visualisations that deliver actionable insights. Ability to relate to and work with technical and non-technical staff at every level of the School. Ability to provide training and support to peers and end-users in-person and online. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, hybrid working, and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the “contact us” links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email Planning.Division@lse.ac.uk . The closing date for receipt of applications is 15 November 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Planning Officer (Power BI Developer) Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 07/10/2026 Closing date: 15/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site 