    "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/6834/0/474984/15539/assistant-professor-in-accounting": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Accounting",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Accounting Register Login Back to search results Assistant Professor in Accounting LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university As an equal opportunities employer strongly committed to diversity and inclusion, we encourage applications from women and those of Minority Ethnic backgrounds as they are currently under-represented at this level in this area. All appointments will be made on merit or skill and experience relative to the role. Department of Accounting Assistant Professor in Accounting The Department of Accounting at LSE invites applications from outstanding candidates for the post of Assistant Professor in Accounting. Those specialising in any area of accounting are encouraged to apply, although when making recruiting decisions we will take into account teaching needs and priority areas as the ongoing development of the department and composition of the faculty may require. For further information on the department, see https://www.lse.ac.uk/accounting/about-us . Candidates will have: · A completed PhD, or be close to obtaining a PhD, in accounting, or related area, by the post start date . · A clear, well developed and viable strategy for outstanding research that has the potential to result in leading publications in accounting. · Ability to teach accounting at under- and post-graduate level, ideally evidenced by prior experience in teaching. Further specific criteria that will be used when shortlisting for this post can be found on the person specification, which is attached to this vacancy on the LSE’s online recruitment system. Candidates will also be expected to make relevant service and citizenship contributions as appropriate for early-career colleagues. The appointment is expected to commence no later than 1 September 2027. In addition to a competitive salary the benefits that come with this job include an occupational pension scheme, a research grants policy with personal reward options, generous research leave (sabbatical) entitlement, a collegial faculty environment and excellent support, training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the How-to-Apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries about applying via the online system, please use the “contact us” links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. If you have queries about the role, please email the Department Manager, Yvonne Guthrie ( y.guthrie@lse.ac.uk ) . The closing date for receipt of applications is 6 November 2026 (23.59 UK time). We are unable to accept any late applications. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to give a presentation and meet with the faculty. Apply now Back to search results Assistant Professor in Accounting Job Type: Academic Posted: 28/09/2026 Closing date: 06/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
    },
    "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/1996/0/475539/15539/country-economist-jordan": {
      "title": "Country Economist Jordan",
      "description": "Country Economist Jordan Register Login Back to search results Country Economist Jordan LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university. The International Growth Centre (IGC) Country Economist Jordan Salaries will be commensurate with experience, taking into account pay equity within the Centre. Salary is no less than £50,000 gross per annum plus 10% of retirement contribution supplement and inclusive of allowances The International Growth Centre (IGC) works with policymakers in developing countries to promote inclusive and sustainable growth through pathbreaking research. We are a global research centre with a network of world-leading researchers and in-country teams and initiatives working across Africa, South Asia, and the Middle East. Based at LSE and in partnership with the University of Oxford, Addis Ababa University (AAU) and the Lahore University of Management Sciences (LUMS), we are majority funded by the UK Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office (FCDO). We work to improve the productivity of people and firms as the key driver of sustainable economic development. The IGC has embedded Country Economists in its partner countries which currently include Bangladesh, Ethiopia, India, Jordan, Mozambique, Pakistan, Sierra Leone and Zambia, as well as Flexible Engagement programmes including the Caribbean, Tanzania, Nepal and South Africa. The IGC is currently seeking a Country Economist or Country Economist Jordan based in Amman. Country Economists are a key part of the IGC’s in-country presence, working under the leadership of the Country Director and Lead Academic to deliver the country strategy and connect local policy priorities with global research expertise. The role combines policy engagement, analytical work and programme delivery: building strong relationships with government, researchers, development partners and other stakeholders; identifying and supporting policy-relevant research opportunities; producing high-quality policy analysis and written outputs; and helping translate research into policy influence through meetings, events and wider communications. Country Economists also contribute to the effective management, monitoring and evaluation of the country programme, ensuring that activities remain responsive to local priorities and contribute to meaningful policy impact. Applicants should have strong economics skills, excellent quantitative skills in economic analysis, a sophisticated understanding of economic policy, and hold a post-graduate degree in economics, public policy, or a related discipline. Successful applicants will be dynamic self-starters with excellent written and oral communication skills. They will also demonstrate a team-oriented, respectful and collaborative approach to working with others. Fluency in Arabic is required. For further information about the posts, please see the how to apply document , CE job description and person specification . To apply for this post, please go to https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/ . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the “contact us” links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. If you have queries about the role, please email Vivian Bronsoler Nurko on v.bronsoler-nurko@lse.ac.uk To find out more about the position and International Growth Centre, please go to https://www.theigc.org/about/careers/ The closing date for applications is 30 October 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept late applications. Apply now Back to search results Country Economist Jordan Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 09/10/2026 Closing date: 30/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. View our privacy policy Cookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Services Always Act