    "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/1066/0/474023/15539/business-applications-specialist": {
      "title": "Business Applications Specialist",
      "description": "Business Applications Specialist Register Login Back to search results Business Applications Specialist LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university Data and Technology Services Business Applications Specialist Salary from £53,949 pa to £62,160 pa inclusive with potential to progress to £69,073 pa inclusive of London allowance This is a fixed term appointment for one year The London School of Economics is a cosmopolitan university situated in the vibrant centre of London specialising in the study of social sciences. Our Data and Technology Services division provides services to 14,000 staff and student users. Working with product owners and other team members to maintain and optimise business applications throughout the service life cycle ensuring continual service improvement. They will support reporting tools and systems to enable accurate management reporting as well as the incident management of issues relating to integrations between applications and database services. They will take the lead on maintenance projects, subject matter expertise and third line support within the maintenance and operational plans for systems related to application services, integrations between databases and applications and reporting infrastructure. Initially this role will focus on implementation of LSEs digital experience platform for first 12 months. Working as part of the Product/Project team acting as technical lead within the Digital Communications team and external partner to ensure the successful delivery of a school Intranet. The Business Application Specialist will: Work closely with service owners to understand application roadmaps ensuring best value from available products Ensure continual service improvement through in particular: - Automation of repetitive support tasks - Remote management of systems to monitor performance and respond to alerts - Devolving support tasks to front line services or service lines to improve efficiency of the service - Identifying opportunities for enhancing productivity and the user experience - Ensure maintained services are patched and secure according to required security standards (Cyber Essentials +) where applicable Maintain reference documentation such as schematics, technical guidelines, operational standards and details of IT assets Provide subject matter expertise on business application services to the LSE, including providing technical expertise to support decision making Candidates should have: Experience with managing server and software configurations including Apache/Tomcat/SSL Certificates/IIS etc. Knowledge of the install upgrade maintenance and support of third-party applications, supporting business functions such as HR, Finance and Student Lifecycle Management Ability to utilise scripting languages and tools (e.g., Javascript, CSS/HTML, Python, PowerShell) Evidence of a strong technical background relating to industry standard technology (Linux/Windows/MS SQL/Oracle) Ability to communicate complex ideas and technical issues to a range of different non-technical audiences. Able to interpret user requirements offering solutions that offer an exceptional user experience and meet business needs Able to plan own work and deliver effective, agreed outcomes as per scheduled. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, hybrid working, and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the “contact us” links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email dts.admin@lse.ac.uk . The closing date for receipt of applications is 26 October 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Business Applications Specialist Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 09/10/2026 Closing date: 26/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
