    "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/4179/0/475329/15539/research-assistant": {
      "title": "Research Assistant",
      "description": "Research Assistant Register Login Back to search results Research Assistant LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university Management Research Assistant Salary from £36,513 to £41,565 pa inclusive with potential to progress to £44,468 pa inclusive of London allowance Funding is available to support this position for 12 months The post supports a research programme lead by Dr. Raúl Sánchez De La Sierra from LSE’s Department of Management. The research programme concerns armed groups, state formation, and governance in the eastern De mocratic Republic of Congo. This is a field-intensive post. The post holder will spend roughly half of each year in North and South Kivu, including in remote artisanal mining areas several hours or days from the nearest town, reached by motorbike or on foot. Main duties and responsibilities include identifying appropriate methods of investigation or analysis according to data and objectives; conveying complex conceptual ideas or complex information which may be highly detailed, technical or specialist; interpreting and analysing patterns or trends in data; managing large scale databases. Candidates should have a completed Master or Bachelor’s degree (or equivalent) in economics or other closely related quantitative discipline; graduate degree in economics or public policy that includes graduate level coursework in econometrics as well as in political economy, or Maters-level economics research training; knowledge of the research literature on the political economy of conflict and armed group governance; experience in cleaning and managing large survey and administrative datasets; proficiency in Stata, R, or Python; resilience to work for extended periods in a remote insecure setting . We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, hybrid working, and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the “contact us” links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email R.Sanchez-De-La-Sierra@lse.ac.uk . The closing date for receipt of applications is 21 October 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Research Assistant Job Type: Research Posted: 05/10/2026 Closing date: 21/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (BST) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
