    "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/4711/0/475070/15539/senior-technical-business-analyst-ai-automation": {
      "title": "Senior Technical Business Analyst (AI / Automation)",
      "description": "Senior Technical Business Analyst (AI / Automation) Register Login Back to search results Senior Technical Business Analyst (AI / Automation) LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university Data and Technology Services Senior Technical Business Analyst (AI / Automation) Salary from £53,949 to £62,160 pa inclusive with potential to progress to £69,073 pa inclusive of London allowance This is a fixed term appointment for 3 years. The London School of Economics is a cosmopolitan university situated in the vibrant centre of London that specialises in the study of social sciences. Our Data and Technology Services division provides services to over 14,000 staff and student users. Data and Technology Services (DTS) delivers technology enabled business change with a focus ranging from strategic and operational business outcomes to service improvements of incumbent services. The scope of DTS projects spans from infrastructure technologies and strategic systems to business processes within end user facing services. The postholder will report into the Lead Technical Business Analyst. This is a hands-on role. Key responsibilities include business and technical analysis with the AI/Automation team, with the postholder working directly with business and technical stakeholders to understand problems, elicit and challenge requirements, analyse processes and data flows, develop solution options, and translate business needs into clear requirements for technical delivery teams. The role requires the postholder to personally lead requirements elicitation activities, support testing and service transition, and contribute to business change required for LSE to maximise measurable business benefits and outcomes. The postholder will be responsible for researching and understating business needs being addressed by the product team, current technology environment, and utilising incoming technology solutions to develop solutions and/or service(s) that bridge gap between the current and desired states, whilst ensuring the team is solving the right problem with the right tools and approach. Candidates should have/be: Significant experience in authoring high quality documentation for business analysis activities, including business requirements, options analysis, process design BPMN 2.0 , user stories, test scripts and acceptance criteria for a technical system delivery Able to gather and interpret user requirements and produce viable user-centric solutions in accordance with regulatory requirements platform governance (e.g. data protection, access controls, environment strategy) and School policies and procedures. Ability to convert business requirements into user stories, use cases, process models (e.g. BPMN), data models and technical specifications, and support solution validation through prototypes or iterative refinement Able to proactively identify and manage risks, issues and dependencies, proposing effective mitigation strategies We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, hybrid working, and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the “contact us” links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email dts.admin@lse.ac.uk The closing date for receipt of applications is 21 October 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Senior Technical Business Analyst (AI / Automation) Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 29/09/2026 Closing date: 21/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (BST) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. View our privacy policy Cookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Services Always Active These Services are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Functional Services Functional Services With these services, the website is able to provide advanced functionality and personalization. They may be set by us or by third parties whose services we use on our sites. If you do not allow these services, this website may not function properly. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject All Confirm My Choices 1 Technical Support Today New Messages Technical Support Chatbot (with creds) a few seconds ago Welcome to Technical Support. Please could you let us know whether you're a candidate or a recruiter? Candidate Recruiter ⚡ by Freshworks 1"
