    "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/5337/0/475037/15539/partnerships-and-student-recruitment-manager": {
      "title": "Partnerships and Student Recruitment Manager",
      "description": "Partnerships and Student Recruitment Manager Register Login Back to search results Partnerships and Student Recruitment Manager LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university LSE Extended Education Partnerships and Student Recruitment Manager Salary from £43,277 to £51,714 pa inclusive of London allowance If you have a track record in student recruitment and in building effective international partnerships, this is an opportunity to join an ambitious team and help deliver growth for the LSE Summer School. Reporting to the Associate Director of Marketing and Recruitment, you will oversee the design and execution of recruitment plans for the LSE Summer School. The role combines student recruitment activity with building and maintaining relationships with selected universities, and will work closely with colleagues across marketing, admissions, and business development. You will lead the planning and delivery of recruitment activity across international, UK and virtual channels; monitor performance against KPIs; and use market insight, application data and partner feedback to guide efforts. You will also manage the recruitment budget, coordinate trips and events, oversee student ambassador activity, and line manage one direct report. We are looking for a self-starter with excellent organisation, communication and stakeholder management skills. You will be confident working with partners and colleagues at different levels, creative in developing recruitment initiatives, and analytical in evaluating their effectiveness. Experience in Higher Education and a genuine interest in the international education market are highly desirable. Candidates should be able to demonstrate the following key attributes: Experience of delivering student recruitment plans and initiatives that achieve results Experience of building and maintaining effective relationships with international partners and working across cultures Strong analytical skills, with the ability to evaluate performance and present data and reports clearly and succinctly Experience of using CRM systems to support recruitment activity and of managing budgets effectively Excellent communication, presentation and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to influence, collaborate and facilitate action Excellent organisation, attention to detail and the ability to manage competing priorities and deadlines The Extended Education division is a successful and commercially focused division. The courses, degrees and diplomas we offer across this diverse and dynamic portfolio provide a significant revenue source for the school, generating critical funds to invest in LSE’s world-leading teaching and research. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave and excellent training and development opportunities. This role is based on our central London campus. Flexible working arrangements are supported within the team. To ensure effective collaboration, stakeholder engagement and an excellent student experience, team members are expected to work on campus for a minimum of three days per week. During the Summer School delivery period, when the level of operational activity and on-campus engagement increases, this rises to four days per week. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.lse.ac.uk/LSEJobs . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the “contact us” links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email Lisa Lind Havdahl ( l.l.havdahl@lse.ac.uk ). The closing date for receipt of applications is Sunday 18 October (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Partnerships and Student Recruitment Manager Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 29/09/2026 Closing date: 18/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (BST) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. View our privacy policy Cookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your r