    "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/6968/0/473246/15539/power-apps-developer-analyst": {
      "title": "Power Apps Developer Analyst",
      "description": "Power Apps Developer Analyst Register Login Back to search results Power Apps Developer Analyst LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university Data and Technology Services Power Apps Developer Analyst Salary from £43,277 to £51,714 pa inclusive with potential to progress to £55,497 pa inclusive of London allowance LSE is one of the leading social science\nuniversities in the world, ranked among the top universities\nnationally and internationally. The School is synonymous\nwith quality, progressive thinking and delivering excellence. We use Power Apps and\nM365 Power Platform suite of products and related services to\nenable us to build custom business applications quickly and easily to support our business processes for our salaried\nand hourly staff lifecycle.  We need an\nexperienced analyst to develop and maintain Power Apps so that we can continue\nto offer excellent service to our users. You will have experience in: Microsoft Power\n    Platform development including Power Automate, and experience of working in DevOps environment to support\n    Power Apps solutions as M365 Power Platform Admin and developer following\n    the AML framework. Creating and\n    maintaining workflows using Power Automate, and Experience of connecting PowerApps with\n    SharePoint and integrating other solutions using standard connectors. You will also have: An excellent working knowledge\n    of complex Excel formulas, The ability to identify,\n    analyse and document business requirements, and Knowledge of configuring\n    ETL tools and/or ability to write code to automate data flows using API to\n    various systems as part of automation/process improvement. Ability to identify AI services for app development,\n    such as Copilot Studio In return, we offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual\nleave, hybrid working and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the “contact us” links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email dts.admin@lse.ac.uk. The closing date for\nreceipt of applications is 15 October 2026 (23:55 UK time). Regrettably,\nwe are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Power Apps Developer Analyst Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 01/10/2026 Closing date: 15/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (BST) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agr