    "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/5377/0/475057/15539/programme-administrator": {
      "title": "Programme Administrator",
      "description": "Programme Administrator Register Login Back to search results Programme Administrator The LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university. School of Public Policy Programme Administrator Salary from £36,513 to £41,565 with potential to progress to £44,468 pa inclusive of London allowance. This is a fixed term post until October 2027. The LSE School of Public Policy equips students with the skills and ideas to transform people and societies. We are an international community where ideas and practice meet, creating professionals with the ability to analyse, understand and resolve the challenges of contemporary governance. We are now seeking to appoint a highly committed and motivated Programme Administrator to provide high quality and comprehensive administrative support to staff and students on our postgraduate degree programmes. The postholder will have responsibilities for one or more programmes according to operational need. This role will involve you working closely with staff and students in a fast paced and dynamic work environment. The post-holder will play a pivotal role in the smooth and efficient running of the designated programme/s. You will collaborate with key academic and professional services staff to proactively develop the programme/s, student experience and learning community. R esponsibilities will include acting as a focal point of contact for student and applicant enquiries, course administration, editing online learning resources, and coordination of assessments and examinations. You will be responsible for detailed planning of programme logistics and events, contributing to the student lifecycle from Welcome (induction) to graduation, and interaction with LSE’s central services to deliver a seamless student experience. You should possess relevant administration and customer service (student-facing) experience within higher education. You will also have excellent oral and written communication skills, the ability to work under your own initiative as well as within a team, and excellent IT skills. A commitment to excellence in service delivery to students and colleagues is essential. This is an exciting opportunity for an enthusiastic and organised administrator to join a busy and friendly team. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, hybrid working, and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the “contact us” links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email j.swallow@lse.ac.uk . The closing date for receipt of applications is 14 October 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Apply now Back to search results Programme Administrator Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 29/09/2026 Closing date: 14/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (BST) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I ha