    "https://jobs.lse.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/3659/0/475008/15539/research-coordinator": {
      "title": "Research Coordinator",
      "description": "Research Coordinator Register Login Back to search results Research Coordinator LSE is committed to building a diverse, equitable and truly inclusive university Department of Sociology Research Coordinator Salary from £36,513 to £41,565 pa inclusive with potential to progress to £44,468 pa inclusive of London allowance This is initially a full-time fixed term appointment for three years, with further extension subject to funding. LSE Sociology is seeking a dedicated and professional Research Coordinator to support the Department’s research administration and the Sociology MPhil/PhD programme. Working under the direction of the Department Research Manager, the post-holder will assist with the coordination of research activities, strategic initiatives and formal research assessment exercises. They will help promote a vibrant research culture, support funding-related activity, administer academic visitor and research staffing processes, and contribute to the successful delivery of seminars, conferences and other research events. A substantial part of the role will involve providing comprehensive administrative support for the Sociology MPhil/PhD programme, including admissions, programme delivery, examinations and assessments, communications, records, student support, events, facilities and liaison with the PhD Academy. The successful candidate will bring excellent administrative and organisational skills, strong attention to detail and the ability to work accurately across competing priorities. They will have experience of administration in Higher Education, with confidence in communicating professionally with staff, students and external contacts. They will be proactive, flexible and collaborative, with the judgement to use initiative, follow procedures consistently and refer issues appropriately. We offer an occupational pension scheme, generous annual leave, hybrid working, and excellent training and development opportunities. For further information about the post, please see the how to apply document , job description and the person specification . To apply for this post, please go to www.jobs.lse.ac.uk . If you have any technical queries with applying on the online system, please use the “contact us” links at the bottom of the LSE Jobs page. Should you have any queries about the role, please email sociology.admin@lse.ac.uk . The closing date for receipt of applications is 13 October 2026 (23.59 UK time). Regrettably, we are unable to accept any late applications. Interviews are expected to take place on 27 October 2026. Apply now Back to search results Research Coordinator Job Type: Professional Services Posted: 29/09/2026 Closing date: 13/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (BST) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Baroness Baron Doctor Father Lady Lord Miss Mr Mrs Ms Professor Dame Professor Professor Lord Professor Sir Reverend Sir Other Dame Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
